= Solution
{parent=c}

The <von Mangoldt function> is nonnegative and satisfies $\Lambda(m)\leq\log m$. Using the <von Mangoldt divisor identity>,
$$
(\Lambda*\Lambda)(n)
=\sum_{d\mid n}\Lambda(d)\Lambda(n/d)
\leq\sum_{d\mid n}\Lambda(d)\log(n/d)
\leq\log n\sum_{d\mid n}\Lambda(d)
=(\log n)^2.
$$

For $0<u\leq1$, a comparison with an <improper integral> gives
$$
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{(\log n)^2}{n^{1+u}}
\ll1+\int_1^\infty\frac{(\log t)^2}{t^{1+u}}\,dt
=1+\frac2{u^3}
\ll u^{-3}.
$$

